# The Ancient One (descend 8): "can't attack or block unless there are eight or more permanent cards in your graveyard". Bot1 casts it
# on turn 1 and, with Thought Scours (each mills two cards, the Scours themselves are instants and no permanent cards) fills its
# graveyard: turn 3 it holds seven permanent cards (a Lightning Bolt milled with them is an instant and no permanent card): it cannot
# attack (turn 3) nor block Bot2's Grizzly Bears (turn 4). On turn 5 it pays {2}{U}{B} to draw and discard a Hill Giant: an eighth
# permanent card, and on turn 6 it blocks and kills the Bears (damage 8 to a 2/2), on turn 7 it attacks. The activation's reflexive
# ability (CR 603.12): Bot2 is the target player and mills four, the Hill Giant's mana value (CR 202.3), Bot2 takes the
# eight on turn 7. Bot1's Ornithopter keeps the engine asking about attackers and blockers. CR 207.2c, 110.4a, 508.1c, 509.1b.

